 ## Overview
-Spatial and nD transforms allow the application of geometric transformations (rotation, translation, scaling, and permutation) to Signed Distance Field (SDF) primitives and discrete data structures by applying the inverse transformation to the query point rather than transforming the geometry itself [S1, S2, unofficial]. This approach ensures that the underlying data structures remain unmodified, preserving local linearity and allowing constant-time affine queries per dimension [S1, unofficial]. It differs from direct geometry transformation by deferring the coordinate change to the evaluation step, which avoids distorting the stored data and supports non-uniform or spatially varying distortions [S2, unofficial].
